-- The claimant's side of the same relation: where the limited liability company has had to give that agreement, process in a proceeding of the kind
-- the agreement covers may be served on the Secretary of State as its agent (fork F7: "may be served" is read as following from the agreement).
-- src:1322 | it shall agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or limited liability company of this State, as well as for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to the provisions of § 262 of this title, and shall irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN form IS A `dg8 Form of a combination`
      `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is to enforce an obligation of a constituent corporation or limited liability company of this State, or an obligation of the surviving or resulting limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) process may be served on the Secretary of State as agent of the surviving or resulting limited liability company` MEANS
        `s 264(d) the surviving or resulting limited liability company must agree to be served with process in this State` form `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`
    AND `the proceeding is to enforce an obligation of a constituent corporation or limited liability company of this State, or an obligation of the surviving or resulting limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation`

-- Service by electronic transmission is permitted "but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State". (What the Secretary of State prescribes is outside the inputs.)
-- src:1322 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. The Secretary of State is authorized to issue such rules and regulations with respect to such service as the Secretary of State deems necessary or appropriate. In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company thereof by letter, directed to such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address so designated. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served upon the Secretary of State, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the process is served by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is served as prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the means of serving process on the Secretary of State is permitted` MEANS
        (NOT `the process is served by electronic transmission`)
    OR  `it is served as prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- The Secretary of State must notify the survivor by letter "forthwith" (the text fixes no number of days, so no date is computed).
-- src:1322 | In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company thereof by letter, directed to such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address so designated. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `process has been served upon the Secretary of State in accordance with the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the Secretary of State must forthwith notify the surviving or resulting limited liability company by letter` MEANS
    `process has been served upon the Secretary of State in accordance with the subsection`

-- The letter goes to the address specified in the agreement, unless the survivor has designated in writing a different address, in which
-- case it goes to the last address so designated.
-- src:1322 | directed to such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address so designated. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the address the surviving or resulting limited liability company specified` IS A STRING
      `the different addresses it has since designated in writing, oldest first` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 264(d) the address to which the Secretary of State must mail the letter` MEANS
    IF null `the different addresses it has since designated in writing, oldest first`
    THEN `the address the surviving or resulting limited liability company specified`
    ELSE at `the different addresses it has since designated in writing, oldest first` (count `the different addresses it has since designated in writing, oldest first` MINUS 1)

-- How the letter is sent and what it encloses.
-- src:1322 | Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the letter is sent as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient`
    AND `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State`

-- The plaintiff's duty on such service: to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service
-- is being effected under the subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11, an input).
-- src:1322 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the plaintiff served process and any other papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under § 391(a)(29)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires of a plaintiff` MEANS
        `the plaintiff served process and any other papers in duplicate`
    AND `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to the subsection`
    AND `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under § 391(a)(29)`

-- The fee "shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein".
-- src:1322 | which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served upon the Secretary of State, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` MEANS
    `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding`

-- The Secretary of State "shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process":
-- the duty to retain ends after the day that is 5 years after receipt (fork F8: the fifth anniversary itself is still inside the 5 years).
-- src:1322 | The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d) (src:1322)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(d) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of service` MEANS
    `the day in question` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in years` 5) `after` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process`)

§ `s 264(e) Provisions applied by reference`

-- src:1323 | Sections 251(d)-(f), 255(c) (second sentence) and (d)-(f), 259-261 and 328 of this title shall, insofar as they are applicable, apply to mergers or consolidations between corporations and limited liability companies.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(e) (src:1323)
DECLARE `s 264(e) Provision applied by reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 251(d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e)`
    `s 255(c) second sentence and (d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e)`
    `ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 264(e)`
    `s 328 as applied by s 264(e)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(e) (src:1323)
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 264(e) Provision applied by reference`
`s 264(e) the provisions that apply to mergers or consolidations between corporations and limited liability companies` MEANS
    LIST `s 251(d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e)`
       , `s 255(c) second sentence and (d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e)`
       , `ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 264(e)`
       , `s 328 as applied by s 264(e)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(e) (src:1323)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 264(e) Provision applied by reference`
      `the provision is applicable to the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(e) the provision applies to the merger or consolidation` MEANS
        elem provision (`s 264(e) the provisions that apply to mergers or consolidations between corporations and limited liability companies`)
    AND `the provision is applicable to the merger or consolidation`

§ `s 264(f) Charitable nonstock corporations`

-- Nothing in the section authorizes the merger of a charitable nonstock corporation into a limited liability company if its charitable status would
-- thereby be lost or impaired. Whether the status would be lost or impaired is a plain input: the text names nobody who decides it (fork F9).
-- src:1324 | (f) Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorize the merger of a charitable nonstock corporation into a limited liability company, if the charitable status of such nonstock corporation would thereby be lost or impaired; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(f) (src:1324)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the corporation would be merged into the limited liability company and would not continue as the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its charitable status would thereby be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(f) the section does not authorize the merger of the charitable nonstock corporation into the limited liability company` MEANS
        `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` kind
    AND `the corporation would be merged into the limited liability company and would not continue as the surviving corporation`
    AND `its charitable status would thereby be lost or impaired`

-- "but a limited liability company may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation which shall continue as the surviving corporation."
-- src:1324 | but a limited liability company may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation which shall continue as the surviving corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(f) (src:1324)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the charitable nonstock corporation continues as the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 264(f) the limited liability company may be merged into the charitable nonstock corporation` MEANS
        `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` kind
    AND `the charitable nonstock corporation continues as the surviving corporation`
